menu "RoboHub AVR Platform"

config ROBOHUB_AVR
    bool "Enable the RoboHub AVR platform"
    default y
    help
      Implementations of the RoboHub HAL interfaces on an 8-bit AVR part. A
      project that depends on robohub-avr needs this; a project on another
      platform does not.

config ROBOHUB_AVR_ASSERT
    bool "Check driver arguments and report failures"
    default y
    help
      Have the HAL implementations reject an invalid argument with
      ROBOHUB_ERR_INVALID_ARG rather than writing to a peripheral that was not
      configured. A driver that does not check is faster; a driver that does not
      check turns a wiring mistake into a silent wrong answer.

# The per-driver symbols live in robohub-common, which owns the interfaces, and
# are not sourced from here: the build passes each fragment to the generator
# explicitly, and a fragment that was both sourced and passed would be defined
# twice by anything that follows the sources.

endmenu
